  "description": "TOHYOH crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H68 Co4 Dy8 N50 O50 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),8(C1 H4 O1),10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.658-4.055 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.95-116.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy(pyzic){Dy3Co2(pyzha)6(*pyzha)(NO3)2(H2O)(MeOH)2}]2·(NO3)2·10H2O·8MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
